      "content": "Yes, in linguistics and phonetics that sensation is called **pitch**, and the energy is referred to as **fundamental frequency**. The vibrating vocal cords create a periodic vibration known as **voicing**, which carries the sound wave into your throat as the physical sensation you described. While the place of articulation (how the sound is made) remains the same for both sounds, this difference in pitch and energy is what phonologists use to contrast vowel sounds and stop consonants like /b/ and /p/.",
